// Single source of truth for FULL COURT's real crowd audio — the loud-arena
// layer that makes door-to-door selling FEEL like a packed basketball game.
//
// Three kinds, all REAL ElevenLabs sound-effect mp3s under
// /audio/fullcourt/crowd/ (generated by scripts/bake-fullcourt-crowd.js):
//
//   CHEERS (5 × 15s) — the whole arena ERUPTS. Fires every time a door-to-door
//                      SALE lands (the bucket) and on the final buzzer. Picked
//                      at random so a big day never repeats the same roar.
//   HYPE   (4 × 15s) — rhythmic get-loud crowd chants behind the 📣 GET LOUD
//                      button. Hit it in a lull and the building gets you going
//                      again — "DEE-FENSE", "LET'S GO", a drumline, the organ
//                      CHARGE. Random, no immediate repeat.
//   STINGERS (short) — real one-shots for real-game punctuation: an air horn on
//                      TARGET SMASHED / GET LOUD, a ref whistle on the buzzer.
//
// Every prompt is written for a text-to-sound model: name the SOUND, the space
// (huge indoor arena), and the energy. `secs` drives duration_seconds (max 22);
// `influence` is prompt_influence (higher = literal, lower = more musical).
//
// Runtime never hard-depends on these files: sfx.playCrowdSample falls back to
// the synth sfxCrowdRoar if an mp3 is missing, so it is never silent.
//
// To (re)generate after editing a prompt:  node scripts/bake-fullcourt-crowd.js
// Short samples first:                      node scripts/bake-fullcourt-crowd.js --audition

